Three remaining defects, all **high / blocker**:

1. **R12-N33 — Ignored symlinks bypass dependency alias detection.**  
   `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:135` checks tracked symlinks only. With an ignored `link -> a` and self-contained `b` declaring `dependsOn:["link/input"]`, a committed change to `a/input` selects `a` but misses `b`. The dependency is clean and ASCII, status remains clean, and no guard resolves its physical identity. Consequently, `b` can carry a stale pass while reading its explicitly declared dependency. Resolve dependency paths and their existing ancestors physically, including ignored symlinks. Established by source trace; scratch reproduction was unavailable.

2. **R12-N34 — Returning HEAD to its starting commit hides intervening movement.**  
   `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1436` compares only the starting and ending commits. If another process changes `H → H′`, a check observes the fixed input at `H′`, and HEAD returns to `H` before completion, `material_clean` remains true. The pass and material bindings are attributed to `H` and become eligible for carry. This violates R2’s requirement that HEAD did not move during validation. Validate an immutable checkout or otherwise detect intervening changes. Established by source trace; this sequence was not newly executed.

3. **R12-N35 — The first Unicode filename can conceal case folding.**  
   `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:518` returns after its first usable entry. In a Unicode case-folded directory, an entry `0ı` swaps to `0I`, but those names need not alias; ASCII `a` and `A` still do. Thus, a folded `shared` directory containing `0ı` and a case-sensitive child `shared/a` can pass the probe. With modules `shared/a` and `b`, and `b` depending on ASCII path `shared/A/input`, changing `shared/a/input` can carry `b`. The ASCII guards do not constrain probe entries. Use a probe whose negative result establishes the required lookup behavior. Established by source trace and Python’s Unicode case-fold model; matching filesystem hardware was not exercised.

Targeted carry/selection tests, the delivery-reader test, and `go vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose` passed. The module-wide strict run failed because the sandbox denied temporary build writes; the full strict run was also attempted but did not complete during this review. Sealed matrix evidence remains green. Assessment commands were omitted because scratch creation was denied and those commands persist files. No repository changes or attestation were made.

Rules applied: POSE review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style, and delivery evidence. The structural ADR maps to D1–D3. The sweep covered all changed runtime files, tests, docs/scaffolds, selection and dependency widening, submodules, aliases, engine identity, metadata, chained carries, cancellation, and canonical publication.

